A||N||3||fierodave||HEADLINER CHEAP FIX!!!!!!!||||14||
Z||000000||fierodave||03-25-2000||11:31 PM||||<BR>HELLO ALL!  been reading about this fiberglass board and wanted to offer this to you!<P>You guys can redo the headliner in your car for under $25.00  <BR>I get the headliner material from a local fabric store  cost is $7.49 a yard, one yard does one headliner.<BR>Take out your old board and remove the old liner and glue, <P>Get a quart of fast dry (1 hour) urethane,  pour and spread it out on both sides and let dry over night!  you will use the whole quart! The next day the board is like a rock. <BR>then just spray glue the material on and install it!<BR>quart of urethane $9.80<BR>material  $7.90  In popular stock GM colors with the foam backing attached.<BR>spray glue at $14.00 (3M super) can  you will use a half a can, and you get it at the fabric store too!<BR>I have done three this week  look super too!  btw  take your visors to a trim shop and have them recovered with the headliner material too!<P>And if you have the sunroof  and break the board getting it out of the car  don't worry,  just take a priority mail flat rate envelope,  cut two pieces the same size and staple them on, one on each side, this will reinforce it.  then just soak the heck out it with the urethane,  Do it out side in a well vented area though.....lol  or you will buzz for a week  lol,  btw  you do not smell the glue or urethane in the car, I would wait one day though on the urethane to dry!!!!!!<BR>FD<BR><p>[This message has been edited by fierodave (edited 03-26-2000).]||||reg||14
Z||000001||DXR_DAD||03-25-2000||11:43 PM||||Good one Dave, I did just that on my 87 coupe your price is right on, also the visors were $11.00 at the shop. It looked like a pro did it. The gray fabric was a dang good match.<P>So to all, Be like Nike   "Just do it"  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||14
